--a portion of the Vedic (Yajus) litera- ture except which the त्रयी exists until the pralaya;
1: वा. ५९. ५७.
here the Rudras partake of the offerings;
2: Br. II. 9. ८४.
sacred to पितृस्;
3: M. २२. ३५.
Citra- karma, the गणेश्वर taught this to Madana;
4: Br. II. ३२. ६३; IV. 7. ४९; ११. ३०-33; ३४. ५२.
japa at Benares leads one to eternal beatitude;
5: M. १८४. ५६.
identified with शिव.
6: वा. ३०. २४४.

(II)--a son of Janamejaya, versed in त्रयी, and a pupil of याज्ञवल्क्य, and also of शौनक; learnt the science of arms from कृप; father of सहस्रानीक (अश्वमे- dhadatta-वि। प्।);
1: भा. IX. २२. ३८-39.
performed अश्वमेध;
2: M. ५०. ६५-6.
asked शौनक about ययाति and his reply;
3: Ib. २५. 3.
anointed by Brahmans;
4: वा. ९९. २५६.
realis- ed आत्मज्ञान from शौनक and attained निर्वाण.
5: Vi. IV. २१. 3-5.

--(see सत्या) a daughter of सत्राजित् (भन्गकार-म्। प्।). The latter had mistakenly suspected कृष्ण of having murdered his brother, and to make amends, gave his daughter in marriage to कृष्ण though अक्रूर and others had sought her hand before. Mother of 6 sons and 4 daughters among whom were भानु and भौमरिका. Terrified at the murder of her father by
1: भा. X. ५६. ३९-44: Br. III. ७१. ५७-80. वा. ९६. ५५-78, २३३: Vi. IV. १३. ७१. १५१, १५४. M. ४५-21: ४७-13-१९ Vi. IV, १३. ६४-6: ३२. 1.
शतधन्वन् (s.v.) she caused the dead body to be preserved in oil and went to हास्तिनपुरम् to inform कृष्ण. Saw Syamantaka with अक्रूर and coveted it. Welcomed to Indraprastha by द्रौपदी;
2: भा. X. ५७. 7-8, ४१ [2]:
narrated to her the circumstances under which she married कृष्ण;
3: Ib. X. ७१. ४२-3: ८३. 9, १४.
went with कृष्ण during his expedition to Naraka's city, and then to Indra's abode. Embraced and blessed by अदिती; complained to कृष्ण that इन्द्राणी did not accord her proper welcome and insisted on the पारिजात being taken to द्वारका. Defeated Kubera who attracted her husband and was praised by कृष्ण for her valour;
4: Ib. X. ५९. 2; ३८-40 [६५ (v) 2, 9-१०], [२८-29], [६६ (v) ११-20]: Vi. IV. १५. ३५: V. २८. 5: २९. १४ and ३५, ३०. २६-7:
observed कल्याणिनि vratam;
5: M. ६९. ६०.
took away the पारिजात; Indra fought for it but was defeated; सत्यभामा gave it back to him saying that she wanted to teach a lesson to इन्द्राणी; returned to द्वारका with the पारिजात presented by Indra.
6: Vi. V. ३०. ३६ to end; ३१. ११.
[page३-514+ ३०]

(I)--one of the seven heavenly worlds;
1: Br. II. १९. १५६: M. ६१. 1.
Brah- maloka, the 7th loka; equal to भूलोक in circumference; six crores of yojanas; in tapolokam; beyond is para and para at long distance;
2: Br. IV. 2. १३, १६, २५, ३८, १४१, १४२-44.
those who go there do not return and are rid of the सम्सार wheel;
3: Ib. IV. 2. ३७.
after residing for several years they get one with the deity नारायण.
4: Ib. II. २१. २२: ३५. २०६-08.

(I)--a wife of पराशर, and mother of व्यास;
1: भा. II. 7. ३६: I. 3. २१: XII. 6. ४९: वा. 1. 2:
in her previous birth अच्छोदा the mind-born daugh- ter of the पितृस्; now born as a fisherwoman, of अद्रिका Matsya at the confluence of the गन्गा and the यमुना;
2: Br. III. १०. ७३-4: M. १४. १९. वा. ७३. २१-2.
her son व्यास, compiled the १८ पुराणस् and the भारत।
3: M. ५३. ७०.

(I)--a sacrifice in नैमिष extending over a thou- sand years;
1: भा. I. 1. 4: वा. 2. १३-14: २३. १९: ५४. 2.
at कुरुक्षेत्र;
2: Br. II. 1. १७.
by Indra for ५०० years.
3: Vi. IV. 5. 1, 3.

--(सत्राजित्-म्। प्।) a son of Nimna (Nighna- ब्र्। and वि। प्।) a friend of God आदित्य; afraid of कृष्ण, be- friended him by bestowing his daughter and the jewel Sya- mantaka on कृष्ण. This jewel was given to him as a present by the Sun god. Wearing it सत्राजित made the citizens of द्वारका blind by its splendour. It was placed in a seperate house to be worshipped as God; refused to part with it when कृष्ण demanded it for the Yadu king. His brother Pra- sena while out a hunting took it to the forest where a lion killed him. जाम्बवन् killed the lion and took the jewel and gave it to his daughter. सत्राजित suspected कृष्ण of killing his brother and depriving him of the jewel. कृष्ण went to the forest, tracked the steps which led to the cave of जाम्बवन्, and after defeating him took his daughter and the jewel to द्वारका. In a public assembly सत्राजित was sent for and the jewel was given to him by कृष्ण. सत्राजित's concern how to befriend कृष्ण. He offered his daughter and the jewel to him. He married the daughter सत्यभामा but returned the jewel to him;
1: भा X. ch. ५६ (whole): IX. २४. १३; Br. III. ७१. २१-60; Vi. V. १३. १०, १४.
married the ten daughters of Kaikeya who gave birth to १०१ sons. the eldest of whom was भङ्गकार;
2: M. ४५. १७, १९.
other members of the family, अक्रूर, शतधन्वा and others who wished to marry सत्यभामा became jealous and plotted to kill सत्राजित्; शतधन्वा mur- [page३-521+ २४] dered him while asleep; in order to avenge his death and also to take the jewel, कृष्ण pursued him and killed him.
3: Vi. IV. १३. ६७-100.

a son of Satyaka;
1: भा. I. १०. १८; IX. २४. १३-14; M. ४५. २२; वा. ९६. ६३; Vi. IV. १४. 2.
followed कृष्ण to हास्तिनपुर and was welcomed. Returned back to द्वारका with him. Followed the वृष्णि host to the city of बाण and fought with कुम्भाण्ड, his minister;
2: भा. I. १३. १६ [1]; X. ५८. 1 and 6, २८; ६३. 3 and 8; [५१ (v) ३०- ३१; ५९. ६३].
learnt the secrets of archery from Arjuna;
3: Ib. III. 1. ३१ and ३५.
defend- ed the western gate of मथुरा, being on the right detach- ment of कृष्ण's army: pursued the retreating enemy to five yojanas and came out successful;
4: Ib. X. ५०. २० [4]; [५० (V) १२], [३०]; [५१ (V) २५].
entered यादव sabha1 with कृष्ण and राम and was honoured. Defended द्वा- रका and expelled साल्व's army;
5: IbX. [४२ (V) १३-14]; ५२ [५६ (V) 1]; ७६. १४; ७७. 4.
went to see the पाण्डवस् at उपप्लाव्य; was consulted by कृष्ण on the eve of his war with जरासन्ध. Joined Yadus in defeating पौण्ड्रक;
6: IbX. ७८ [९५ (V) 2]; [५० (V) 8 and २८].
went with the sacrificial horse of कृष्ण; fought with Aniruddha [page३-579+ २९] at प्रभास;
7: Ib. X. ८९. २२ [2]; XI. ३०. १६.
survived कुरुक्षेत्र war;
8: Ib. X. ८०. [3].
was killed in यादव battle at प्रभास.
9: Vi. V. ३७. ४६.

--that which is above and divine;
1: वा. १०२. ५४.
the mind becomes clean and the truth is open to him and leads to ज्ञानम् or knowledge;
2: Ib. ७४. ७६.
of विष्णु.
3: Ib. ६६. ८७, १०४-6.

--a यादव tribe related to the पाण्डवस्. Their overlord was कृष्ण;
1: भा. 1. 4. 7; १४. २५; II. 4. २०.
knew how to read [page३-580+ २८] others' minds and possessed high understanding and culture;
2: Ib. III. 2. 9.
ended their lives by fighting their own relations;
3: Ib. XI. ३०. १८.
are भाग- vatas;
4: Ib. XII. 8. ४६.
a line of Kings from सात्वत.
5: Vi. IV. १२. ४४.
